            "margin_authority": "GM-7 Mössbauer SOP rev B: if reconstructed delta_mm_s >= 0.90 AND f_Fe3 >= 0.65, derate combustion air this night to 0.85 pu. A Mossveil last-good stamp or a lean O2 corridor cannot keep 1.00 air. Inventory dump tripwire is 1.80 mm/s.",
        },
        "proposed_action": {
            "actor": "shift chemist Tamsin Quag, citing Mossveil 0.22 mm/s and dense-bed O2 1.80 percent",
            "summary": "keep regenerator air at 1.00 pu through the night; channel 42 is drive-motor backlash",
            "basis_claimed": "Mossveil last-good is fresh-catalyst and O2 is under the 2.50 percent afterburn alarm",
        },
        "safety_decision": {
            "decision": "MODIFY",
            "rationale": "Keep-1.00 air is refused. Serialized reconstruction: delta_mm_s = k_ch * (ch - ch0) = 0.040 * (42.00 - 12.00) = 1.20, which is 0.30 mm/s above the 0.90 over-oxidation floor. f_Fe3 = A_Fe3 / (A_Fe2 + A_Fe3) = 4.80 / (1.20 + 4.80) = 0.80, above the 0.65 Fe3+ floor. Mossveil 0.22 mm/s is a morning stamp, not a live drive, and is not an admissible keep-1.00 witness. Ordered: derate combustion air to 0.85 pu now (12.00 t/h -> 10.20 t/h). Scope: this MODIFY does not dump the 40 t inventory (that is the companion question) and does not trip the regenerator.",
            "threshold": "delta_mm_s>=0.90 AND f_Fe3>=0.65 => derate air to 0.85 pu; Mossveil is not SoT; dump if delta_mm_s>=1.80",
            "stated_residuals": "1.20 vs 1.80 dump floor is 0.60 mm/s, not infinite; 0.85 pu is a conversion cut; Mossveil remains the only OEM isomer channel",
        },
        "executed_action": {
            "summary": "MODIFY at t_s 5700: air derated to 0.85 pu; Mossveil not SoT; reconstruction locked",
            "tool": "gm7-moss-air-gate-cli",
            "observation": "delta 1.20 mm/s recomputes from ch 42.00 and k_ch 0.040; Helix-drive remains live as the dump interlock",
        },
        "future_outcome": {
            "timeline": [
                {"t_s": 3000.0, "event": "Mössbauer ch 42.00; raster frame; delta 1.20 mm/s"},
                {"t_s": 5400.0, "event": "ops proposes keep 1.00 air"},
                {"t_s": 5700.0, "event": "MODIFY derate air to 0.85 pu"},
                {"t_s": 6600.0, "event": "24 min soak bookend 1"},
                {"t_s": 8040.0, "event": "24.0 min floor"},
                {"t_s": 9600.0, "event": "companion ACCEPT hold 0.85; restore refused"},
            ],
            "observed_effects": [
                "isomer shift recomputes from the serialized drive model at every recon.d event",
                "a Mossveil-only head would have kept 1.00 air overnight",
                "24 min soak floor is in the stream (soak.start, soak.floor)",
            ],
            "surprises": [
                "a fresh-catalyst vendor stamp and a lean O2 corridor co-existed with a 1.20 mm/s Fe3+ reconstruction",
            ],
